      "raw_text": "To find the total time it took to cook all the food, we need to calculate the cooking time for each ingredient based on the information provided.\n\n**Step 1: Determine the time to cook rice.**\nThe problem states directly: \"It took her 30 minutes to cook rice.\"\n$$ \\text{Time}_{\\text{rice}} = 30 \\text{ minutes} $$\n\n**Step 2: Determine the time to cook pork.**\nThe problem states: \"It took her 20 more minutes to cook pork than rice.\"\n$$ \\text{Time}_{\\text{pork}} = \\text{Time}_{\\text{rice}} + 20 $$\n$$ \\text{Time}_{\\text{pork}} = 30 + 20 = 50 \\text{ minutes} $$\n\n**Step 3: Determine the time to cook beans.**\nThe problem states: \"beans took half the combined cooking time of pork and rice.\"\nFirst, find the combined cooking time of pork and rice:\n$$ \\text{Combined Time} = \\text{Time}_{\\text{pork}} + \\text{Time}_{\\text{rice}} $$\n$$ \\text{Combined Time} = 50 + 30 = 80 \\text{ minutes} $$\n\nNext, calculate half of that combined time:\n$$ \\text{Time}_{\\text{beans}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 80 $$\n$$ \\text{Time}_{\\text{beans}} = 40 \\text{ minutes} $$\n\n**Step 4: Calculate the total cooking time.**\nAdd the cooking times for all three ingredients together:\n$$ \\text{Total Time} = \\text{Time}_{\\text{rice}} + \\text{Time}_{\\text{pork}} + \\text{Time}_{\\text{beans}} $$\n$$ \\text{Total Time} = 30 + 50 + 40 $$\n$$ \\text{Total Time} = 120 \\text{ minutes} $$\n\n#### 120<|im_end|>",
      "answer_text": "To find the total time it took to cook all the food, we need to calculate the cooking time for each ingredient based on the information provided.\n\n**Step 1: Determine the time to cook rice.**\nThe problem states directly: \"It took her 30 minutes to cook rice.\"\n$$ \\text{Time}_{\\text{rice}} = 30 \\text{ minutes} $$\n\n**Step 2: Determine the time to cook pork.**\nThe problem states: \"It took her 20 more minutes to cook pork than rice.\"\n$$ \\text{Time}_{\\text{pork}} = \\text{Time}_{\\text{rice}} + 20 $$\n$$ \\text{Time}_{\\text{pork}} = 30 + 20 = 50 \\text{ minutes} $$\n\n**Step 3: Determine the time to cook beans.**\nThe problem states: \"beans took half the combined cooking time of pork and rice.\"\nFirst, find the combined cooking time of pork and rice:\n$$ \\text{Combined Time} = \\text{Time}_{\\text{pork}} + \\text{Time}_{\\text{rice}} $$\n$$ \\text{Combined Time} = 50 + 30 = 80 \\text{ minutes} $$\n\nNext, calculate half of that combined time:\n$$ \\text{Time}_{\\text{beans}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 80 $$\n$$ \\text{Time}_{\\text{beans}} = 40 \\text{ minutes} $$\n\n**Step 4: Calculate the total cooking time.**\nAdd the cooking times for all three ingredients together:\n$$ \\text{Total Time} = \\text{Time}_{\\text{rice}} + \\text{Time}_{\\text{pork}} + \\text{Time}_{\\text{beans}} $$\n$$ \\text{Total Time} = 30 + 50 + 40 $$\n$$ \\text{Total Time} = 120 \\text{ minutes} $$\n\n#### 120",
